"3R2C building thermal network with equation-based integration (CLIM R06 Ex02)

A single-zone building model with three thermal capacitances (indoor air,
opaque facade, internal masonry walls) coupled through resistances. Outdoor
weather (temperature, south solar irradiance, occupancy factor) is read from
the companion lookup table building_rc_network-week.csv (July sunny week,
tables p.4.12 and 2.23 of the CLIM course).

Ventilation provides the only cooling (no active HVAC). The model integrates
indoor and wall temperatures over one week (168 h) using INTEGRAL.

NOTE: this model intentionally uses INTERPOLATE during time-marching. It is
expected to fail until CoolSolve wires the lookup table store into
IntegralSolver (see docs/integral_table_plan.md). Keep it as a regression
test for that feature.

Source: CLIM R06 repetition exercise 2 (University of Liege), simplified
from the original EES model (variant 2a: constant ventilation, no cooling unit).
"

"--- Geometry and ventilation ---"
Haut = 2.7
Prof = 6
Larg = 4
V_in = Larg * Prof * Haut
V_dot_su_m3h = 60
V_dot_su = V_dot_su_m3h / 3600
rho = 1.2
c_p = 1005
T_su = 14

"--- Internal gains (peak values) ---"
Q_dot_occ_max = 160
Q_dot_light_max = 250
Q_dot_appl_max = 250
SF = 0.5

"--- Integration interval (one week, 600 s output interval) ---"
tau_1 = 0
tau_2 = 604800
N_h = 168
DELTAtau = 600
tau_hour = tau / 3600

"--- Weather from lookup table (July sunny week) ---"
T_out = INTERPOLATE('week', 'tau', 'T_out', tau)
I_dot_south = INTERPOLATE('week', 'tau', 'I_dot_south', tau)
f_occ = INTERPOLATE('week', 'tau', 'f_occ', tau)

"--- Thermal resistances and capacitances ---"
C_opaque = 360000
R_in_1 = 0.1964
R_out_1 = 0.1149
A_opaque = 6.3
U_glazing = 3
A_glazing = 4.5
R_glazing = 1 / U_glazing
h_in = 8
R_w = 0.1429
R_in = 1 / h_in + R_w / 2
A_InternalWalls = Haut * Prof * 2 + Haut * Larg + Prof * Larg * 2
C_InternalWalls = C_opaque / 2
C_in = 5 * V_in * rho * c_p
C_dot_su = V_dot_su * rho * c_p

"--- Initial temperatures [C] ---"
T_in_0 = 25
T_c_in_0 = 25
T_c_wall_0 = 25

"--- State equations (integrated) ---"
T_in = T_in_0 + INTEGRAL(dT_in_dtau, tau, 0, 604800)
T_c_wall = T_c_wall_0 + INTEGRAL(dT_c_wall_dtau, tau, 0, 604800)
T_c_in = T_c_in_0 + INTEGRAL(dT_c_in_dtau, tau, 0, 604800)

dT_in_dtau = Q_dot_capa_in / C_in
dT_c_wall_dtau = Q_dot_capa_c_wall / (C_opaque * A_opaque)
dT_c_in_dtau = Q_dot_capa_c_in / (C_InternalWalls * A_InternalWalls)

"--- Node balances ---"
Q_dot_sens + H_dot_vent + (T_c_in - T_in) / (R_in / A_InternalWalls) + (T_out - T_in) / (R_glazing / A_glazing) + (T_c_wall - T_in) / (R_in_1 / A_opaque) = Q_dot_capa_in

(T_in - T_c_wall) / (R_in_1 / A_opaque) + (T_out - T_c_wall) / (R_out_1 / A_opaque) = Q_dot_capa_c_wall

(T_in - T_c_in) / (R_in / A_InternalWalls) = Q_dot_capa_c_in

"--- Heat flows ---"
H_dot_vent = C_dot_su * (T_su - T_in)
Q_dot_sol = A_glazing * SF * I_dot_south
Q_dot_light = f_occ * Q_dot_light_max
Q_dot_appl = f_occ * Q_dot_appl_max
Q_dot_occ = f_occ * Q_dot_occ_max
Q_dot_clim = 0
Q_dot_sens = Q_dot_clim + Q_dot_light + Q_dot_appl + Q_dot_occ + Q_dot_sol
Q_dot_in_walls = (T_c_wall - T_in) / (R_in_1 / A_opaque) + (T_c_in - T_in) / (R_in / A_InternalWalls)

$IntegralTable tau:600 tau_hour T_c_in T_in T_c_wall T_out Q_dot_in_walls Q_dot_sol Q_dot_sens H_dot_vent Q_dot_capa_in Q_dot_capa_c_wall Q_dot_capa_c_in
